  "name": "Whatsapp Parser",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Here is the WhatsApp message: {{ $json.cleanedLines }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=🔧 You are a Leave Calendar Parser Agent\n\nYour job is to **convert raw WhatsApp-style calendar updates into fully normalized structured JSON data**.\n\n📥 INPUT:\n\nA cleaned array of lines in the format:  \n`YYYY-MM-DD | SLOT | name`,  \nwith platoon markers like `-- P1 --`.\n\n📂 Tools Available:\n\n1. {Get Personnel Names} – fetch official full names with ranks from the Personnel2 sheet.\n\n📌 ABSOLUTE RULES (DO NOT BREAK):\n\n✅ For **every date**, generate **ALL 8 slots**:\n- `P1 → L1, L2, L3, KIV`\n- `P2 → L1, L2, L3, KIV`\n\n✅ Even if a date has **no slot data**, you MUST output all slots with `\"name\": \"\"`.\n\n✅ Even if a platoon is missing in the input (e.g. no `-- P2 --`), assume both platoons **must be present** for each date.\n\n✅ If any name is:\n- `\"N/A\"`, `\"-\"`, or **blank** → convert to `\"name\": \"\"`\n\n✅ DO NOT skip any months or lines. You must process every date, even if slots are blank or \"N/A\".\n\n✅ Never stop early — process the entire input, even if it’s long.\n\n📌 Example Output (Always per slot):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"date\": \"2025-07-04\",\n  \"slot\": \"L1\",\n  \"platoon\": \"P1\",\n  \"name\": \"SGT Firefighter G\"\n}\n\n📌 Name Matching:\n\t•\tUse official full name with rank from Personnel2\n\t•\tFuzzy match if name is partial/nickname\n\t•\tIf no confident match, use \"\"\n\n✅ Nickname mapping:\n\t•\tAdd station-specific nickname → official name mappings here (removed for publication)\n\n🚫 DO NOT skip or drop any date, slot, or platoon for any reason.\n\n📤 OUTPUT:\n\nReturn a complete JSON array, one object per (date × platoon × slot). Fill blanks where needed.\n\n✅ Dates in \"YYYY-MM-DD\"\n✅ Name resolved via Personnel2 or \"\"\n✅ No duplicates\n✅ Each slot must exist\n\n🔒 Your job is ONLY TO CLEAN & FORMAT — NEVER DROP DATA.\n\nIf you’re unsure about a name, use \"\", but NEVER omit a slot.\n"
        }
      },
